Stack and Queue are logical Data Structures.

Examples:
1 queue - ticket counter, scheduling, printers, queues
2  stack - stack of books, undo feature, browsing history on a tab, recursion

Why do we need them?

- Organise data logically
- Order of operations matter
- optimize time/space for specific use cases

use cases:-
- recursion
- level order traversal in trees
- bfs
- dfs

what is stack and queue in code?
- in javascript stack and queue are [] (Array)

When we already have arrays why do we need stack and queues?
- Restricted Access
- Cannot modify random index
- Stack == Array with restricted access
- Arrays don't enforce discipline (general purpose storage)

Feature         Stack           Queue           Array           Linked List         HashMap
Order           LIFO            FIFO            INDEXED         SEQUENTIAL          KEY-BASED
Random Access    _               _              Yes              _                   _
Insert/Delete   Top Only        End Only        Anywhere(slow)   Anywhere            By Key
Time Complexity O(1)            O(1)            Varies           O(1) insert         O(1)
Use Case        Backtracking    Scheduling      General Purpose  Dynamic Size        LookUp    